# License summary 

This software has ONE license, the SciVance Software License (2.3), reproduced
below. You may use the software only while you hold a seat under it. There
are two kinds of seat:

  1. PAID SEAT - for COMMERCIAL USE and for use by or for ANY ORGANIZATION.
     Any use by or for a business, any use with an anticipated commercial
     application, and any use by or for an organization of any kind:
     a government institution, a charity, a school or university, a public
     research, health or safety organization, or any other organization,
     even when the use is noncommercial.
     One seat per developer, perpetual. A team buys one seat for each of its
     developers. Price and how to buy: https://www.GabrielMoraru.com/autopilot

  2. FREE SEAT - for PERSONAL USE by an individual, after you register.
     Personal study, research, hobby projects, done by you for yourself and
     not for any organization. No charge, but you must first register at
     https://www.GabrielMoraru.com/autopilot

PER MAJOR VERSION. A seat, paid or free, is for life for the major version you get it for: a seat for version 2 covers every 2.x release. A later major version (3.0) is not covered; it is a new purchase.

The dividing line is YOU, FOR YOURSELF versus EVERYTHING ELSE. A student
learning on their own uses a free seat; the same student doing a project for
their university needs a paid seat. A freelancer doing paid work needs a
paid seat.

NO REDISTRIBUTION. You may not give the software to anyone else, in any 
form - not even built into your application, unless the conditions below are met. 

The source code of the bridge units is AVAILABLE TO READ AND BUILD, but the
software is not open source: the license below requires a seat and forbids
redistribution, and an OSI-approved open-source license cannot do either.

This summary is not part of the license. Where it differs from the terms
below, the terms below apply.

