# SciVance Software License

## Acceptance

In order to get any license under these terms, you must agree to them as both strict obligations and conditions to all your licenses.

## Seats

You may use the software only while you hold a seat.  Each seat covers one individual developer.

  a. A **paid seat** is bought from the licensor.  It covers any purpose, including commercial use and use by or for a government institution or any other organization.
  b. A **free seat** covers only personal, noncommercial purposes of an individual - see [Noncommercial Purposes](#noncommercial-purposes) and [Organizations](#organizations).  You get a free seat by registering with the licensor at <https://www.GabrielMoraru.com/autopilot>.  The free seat starts when the licensor confirms your registration.  The licensor may decline a registration.

A seat, paid or free, covers the major version of the software it was bought or registered for, including every later release of that major version (for example 2.0, 2.1 and 2.2), with no time limit.  It does not cover a later major version of the software (for example 3.0); that needs a new seat.

## Copyright License

The licensor grants you a copyright license for the software to do everything you might do with the software that would otherwise infringe the licensor's copyright in it for any permitted purpose.  However, you may only distribute the software according to [Distribution](#distribution) and make changes or new works based on the software according to [Changes and New Works License](#changes-and-new-works-license).

## Distribution

**You may not give the software to anyone else.**  You have no license to distribute, publish, sell, lend, mirror, host, or otherwise make the software available to any other person, in any form.  This covers the source code, the compiled unit files (`.dcu`), the executable files, packages, archives, copies of the repository, uploads to a package registry or file-sharing service, and inclusion in any library, component set, template, sample project, course material, training data set, or software development kit.  It covers a changed or derived version of the software exactly as it covers the original.

This also covers an application of your own into which the software is built: you may build and run it for your own use, but you may not give it to any other person, including customers, unless you hold a separate distribution license bought from the licensor.  A seat, paid or free, does not include a distribution license.

One narrow permission, and nothing beyond it:

### 1. Your own application with the bridge inactive

You may give other people an application of your own that you built without the `AUTOPILOT` conditional define.  In such a build the bridge is inactive: it opens no connection and accepts no commands.  This permission does not cover any build made with the `AUTOPILOT` conditional define.  Conditions:

  a. You distribute the application in compiled form - an executable, an installer, a mobile application package, or similar.
  b. What you distribute does not contain the source code of the software, its `.dcu` files, or any other form from which a person could recover the software as a unit reusable in their own projects.
  c. Your own use of the software is covered by a seat - a free seat if your use is personal, a paid seat if it is commercial or by or for any organization.

You owe no credit, notice, or attribution inside your application for this permission.

