The licensor grants you an additional copyright license to make changes and new works based on the source code of the software for any permitted purpose.  **This is for your own use.**  It does not cover the executable files: you may not change them.  [Distribution](#distribution) applies to anything you change or derive exactly as it applies to the original, so a changed version does not become yours to hand out.

## Patent License

The licensor grants you a patent license for the software that covers patent claims the licensor can license, or becomes able to license, that you would infringe by using the software.

## Permitted Purposes

With a paid seat, any purpose is a permitted purpose.  With a free seat, only a noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose.

## Noncommercial Purposes

Any noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose for a free seat, except as limited by [Government Institutions](#government-institutions) and [Organizations](#organizations).

## Government Institutions

Notwithstanding any other section of these terms, use by or for a government institution is **not** a permitted purpose for a free seat, whether or not that use would otherwise be noncommercial and whether or not it would otherwise qualify under [Personal Uses](#personal-uses).  A government institution needs a paid seat for each developer.

## Personal Uses

Personal use for research, experiment, and testing for the benefit of public knowledge, personal study, private entertainment, hobby projects, amateur pursuits, or religious observance, without any anticipated commercial application, is use for a permitted purpose.

## Organizations

Notwithstanding any other section of these terms, use by or for an organization is **not** a permitted purpose for a free seat, whether or not that use would otherwise be noncommercial and whether or not it would otherwise qualify under [Personal Uses](#personal-uses).  This includes any charitable organization, educational institution, public research organization, public safety or health organization, environmental protection organization, association, foundation, or religious organization, regardless of how it is funded.  Such an organization needs a paid seat for each developer.

